From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PixelOS PIF <pif@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] key attestation: recover TEE errors at the Keystore boundary

Keep the SPI path, but also recover eligible Java callers of
KeyStoreSecurityLevel.generateKey when the TEE reports communication failure
or missing attestation keys. Preserve the imported key ID, install the chain
in Keystore and read back its real metadata; remove incomplete imports.

Record the actual backend security level and exclude StrongBox, probe keys,
explicit attestation signers and non-APP namespaces. Keep leaf-only policy
from importing software keys. Resolve an empty/failed package lookup from
the bound local application and log SPI and lower-boundary decisions without
logging aliases, challenges, keybox material or device identifiers.

The November 4 device report establishes absent fallback evidence, not the
exact bypass mechanism. This covers one additional Java boundary and adds
logging to distinguish it on the next build; native Binder callers remain
outside these Java hooks.

---
